{"purpose":"Capture the product intent for parallel container execution: per-repo active containers with a no-dependency gate, so multi-repo projects stop serializing independent work.","content":"## 1. Background\n\nOne EKA project groups several repositories (web, mobile, api) whose knowledge unions in the workspace store, partitioned by provenance source_repo. Execution still allows exactly one active container per project, so independent per-repo plans serialize behind each other even when they share no dependency and run in separate worktrees.\n\n## 2. Users and needs\n\n- As a lead of a multi-repo project, I want per-repo containers to activate in parallel when their plans share no dependency, so web and mobile teams are not blocked by each other.\n- As an operator, I want same-repo activation to stay serialized (exactly-one-active per source_repo), so one worktree never runs two conflicting executions.\n- As an operator, I want cross-repo activation with a plan dependency to refuse with a named reason, so parallel work never silently diverges on dependent plans.\n- As an operator, I want one board per active container plus a summary, so parallel execution stays readable.\n\n## 3. Non-goals\n\n- Cross-project parallelism (out of scope: gate is per project union).\n- Parallel containers in the SAME repo/worktree (refused: one active per source_repo).\n- Automatic dependency inference beyond depends-on/derives-from plan closure."}